# BUGS

A change the file server makes on its own, not through a 9P message (an fsd snapshot's rollback, a post svcd lists in srvfs), makes no event.
A name is cut to 127 bytes.
A watch is not told of changes through another name for the same file (a bind, a symbolic link's target).
Over TCP, VectraOS's client does not ask for `notify`, so a remote mount has none.
